  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 244 PM CDT Mon Oct 12 2026\n\nA dry period is then expected some of Wednesday daytime as surface \nhigh pressure returns to the area briefly. By evening, theta-e \nadvection increases ahead of the approaching upper low off the \nRockies and the lee surface low moves through the region on Thursday \nfollowed by the upper trough with a strong system also coming out of \nCanada later Thursday into Friday. This will bring more widespread \nprecipitation chances from Wednesday night through Thursday. \nTemperatures will be closer to normal and in the 60s to low 70s \nthrough midweek. Then, behind the departing system, stronger cold \nair advection will arrive sending temperatures into the 50s to\nlow 60s for Friday and Saturday and low temperatures in the 30s\nFriday night/Saturday morning. Will need to watch for frost \npotential to start the weekend with a surface high swinging \nthrough. With this high and an upper ridge, conditions are \nlooking drier Friday through the weekend. Friday does look to be\nbreezy to windy which could make it feel even cooler and will \nhave to monitor for any fire weather conditions should there be \nenough time for fuels to dry after the rain on Thursday.",
